1
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,910
- We shouldn't be out here alone. - Why not?

2
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,600
- If your father... - He'll never know we're gone.

3
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:16,640
But if he finds out...

4
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:23,060
You don't need to be afraid of my father.

5
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:51,700
Are you sure?

6
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:53,930
Yes.

7
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:57,550
- We shouldn't go in. - Of course we should.

8
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:44,830
Get out. Get out!

9
00:03:44,950 --> 00:03:46,570
- Let's go. - No.

10
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:48,980
Listen to your friend.

11
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:52,350
They said that you were terrifying

12
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,250
with cat's teeth and three eyes.

13
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,450
You're not terrifying.

14
00:03:59,570 --> 00:04:00,750
You're boring.

15
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:03,470
You don't know what I am.

16
00:04:03,470 --> 00:04:06,930
I know you're a witch and you can see the future.

17
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,030
Tell me mine.

18
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:12,290
Everyone wants to know their future

19
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,260
until they know their future.

20
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:18,000
This is my father's land. My land.

21
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:19,210
Tell me my future

22
00:04:19,210 --> 00:04:23,310
or I'll have your two boring eyes gouged out of your head.

23
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:33,780
Your blood.

24
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,050
Give me a taste.

25
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:04,160
Three questions you get.

26
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:06,990
You won't like the answers.

27
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:13,250
I've been promised to the prince.

28
00:05:14,730 --> 00:05:16,300
When will we marry?

29
00:05:16,490 --> 00:05:18,310
You will never wed the prince.

30
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,070
You will wed the king.

31
00:05:20,410 --> 00:05:21,680
But I will be queen?

32
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,000
Oh, yes.

33
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,590
You'll be queen.

34
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,070
For a time.

35
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:30,910
Then comes another,

36
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:33,210
younger,

37
00:05:33,930 --> 00:05:35,340
more beautiful,

38
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:39,300
to cast you down and take all you hold dear.

39
00:05:40,110 --> 00:05:42,080
W-will the king and I have children?

40
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:46,280
No. The king will have 20 children

41
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,640
and you will have three.

42
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:48,550
That doesn't make sense.

43
00:05:48,550 --> 00:05:50,430
Gold will be their crowns.

44
00:05:52,110 --> 00:05:54,730
Gold their shrouds.

45
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:03,750
Come on, we have to go.

46
00:06:05,550 --> 00:06:07,510
We have to go! Cersei!

47
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,020
Bearers, put it down.

48
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,630
Bearers, up.

49
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,120
Away.

50
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:50,060
Your Grace, we are honored by your presence.

51
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,480
The mourners are waiting.

52
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,880
They will keep waiting.

53
00:06:54,030 --> 00:06:55,610
I want a moment alone with him.

54
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:58,000
But, Your Grace, many of these lords and ladies have travelled

55
00:06:58,010 --> 00:07:00,980
day and night to be here from all seven kingdoms.

56
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,210
They will wait.

57
00:07:29,890 --> 00:07:32,080
He never wanted you to be a Kingsguard,

58
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:34,930
but here you are, protecting his dead body.

59
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:41,470
What he built, it's ours.

60
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:45,550
He built it for us. He meant it for us.

61
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:49,290
They're going to try to take it away.

62
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:50,310
- All of it. - They?

63
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:53,160
All of them out there, our enemies.

64
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:55,970
They're waiting in line to make sure he's really dead.

65
00:07:55,970 --> 00:07:57,900
And as soon as they see the stones on his eyes,

66
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,560
they'll set to work on tearing us apart.

67
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,140
They have nothing to do with it.

68
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:04,610
The man who murdered our father, he tore us apart.

69
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:06,940
He's the enemy. I've been telling you for years.

70
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:08,260
You've been defending him for years.

71
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:09,730
This is exactly what they want.

72
00:08:09,730 --> 00:08:11,600
And now our father is dead

73
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:15,710
and that little monster is out there somewhere drawing breath.

74
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:19,050
Did you set him free?

75
00:08:22,650 --> 00:08:23,840
Tyrion may be a monster,

76
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:27,180
but at least he killed our father on purpose.

77
00:08:28,170 --> 00:08:29,990
You killed him by mistake.

78
00:08:30,050 --> 00:08:31,440
With stupidity.

79
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:35,020
You're a man of action, aren't you?

80
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:37,530
When it occurs to you to do something, you do it.

81
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:39,490
Never mind the consequences.

82
00:08:42,690 --> 00:08:43,790
Take a look.

83
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:46,740
Look at the consequences.

84
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:50,290
Here they are.

85
00:08:54,930 --> 00:08:57,600
He loved you more than anyone in this world.

86
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,800
Apologies.

87
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:45,340
I still don't see why I had to stay

88
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:48,530
in this fucking crate once we set sail.

89
00:10:48,530 --> 00:10:50,100
I saved your life.

90
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:52,700
If they catch you, they catch me.

91
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,110
I cannot say I feel overly guilty

92
00:10:55,110 --> 00:10:57,600
about leaving you in that fucking crate.

93
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,100
Do you know what it's like to stuff your shit

94
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,910
through one of those airholes?

95
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,780
No, I only know what it's like

96
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:06,230
to pick up your shit and throw it overboard.

97
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,850
Pentos?

98
00:11:12,250 --> 00:11:15,400
The home of my colleague Illyrio Mopatis,

99
00:11:15,570 --> 00:11:16,720
a merchant.

100
00:11:16,730 --> 00:11:18,500
He and I met many years ago

101
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:20,340
through mutual friends.

102
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:23,220
A group of people who saw Robert Baratheon

103
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,150
for the disaster he was.

104
00:11:25,650 --> 00:11:28,130
We tried to do what was best for the realm

105
00:11:28,130 --> 00:11:30,570
by supporting a Targaryen restoration.

106
00:11:31,590 --> 00:11:33,970
And thus began the chain of mistakes

107
00:11:33,970 --> 00:11:35,800
that has led us both here.

108
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:39,690
Things have gotten worse, not better.

109
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:43,340
Westeros needs to be saved from itself.

110
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,310
Much better.

111
00:11:50,810 --> 00:11:51,770
My lord?

112
00:11:54,310 --> 00:11:56,770
I don't think I am anymore.

113
00:11:57,710 --> 00:11:58,910
A lord.

114
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:09,720
Are you a lord if you kill your father?

115
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:16,300
I don't imagine they revoke your nobility for killing a whore.

116
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:18,460
It must happen all the time.

117
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:21,110
You already drank yourself across the Narrow Sea.

118
00:12:21,110 --> 00:12:23,100
In a box. Why stop now?

119
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:26,250
Because we are talking about the future of our country.

120
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:32,980
The future is shit.

121
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:37,040
Just like the past.

122
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:45,740
The Sons of the Harpy?

123
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:48,380
Yes, Your Grace. They left it on the body.

124
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:49,800
They've never killed before.

125
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,920
It was only a matter of time, Your Grace.

126
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,840
Conquerors always meet with resistance.

127
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:57,040
I didn't conquer them. Their own people did.

128
00:16:05,310 --> 00:16:07,900
He did not risk his life fighting for his freedom

129
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,910
so cowards in masks could take it away.

130
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:11,930
And I did not take up residence in this pyramid

131
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:15,100
so I could watch the city below decline into chaos.

132
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:17,670
What was the name of the man you lost?

133
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:20,360
White Rat, Your Grace.

134
00:16:21,210 --> 00:16:24,730
I want him buried with honor, publically

135
00:16:25,390 --> 00:16:26,890
in the Temple of the Graces.

136
00:16:27,650 --> 00:16:29,670
The Sons of the Harpy will hear that message.

137
00:16:29,670 --> 00:16:31,350
Make them very angry.

138
00:16:31,350 --> 00:16:33,160
Angry snakes lash out.

139
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:35,820
Makes chopping off their heads that much easier.

140
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:39,340
Find the men who did this and bring them to me.

141
00:16:43,490 --> 00:16:44,230
Your Grace.

142
00:16:58,790 --> 00:16:59,880
Torgo Nudho.

143
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:02,220
Missandei hin Naath.

144
00:17:04,270 --> 00:17:05,920
I wanted to speak with you.

145
00:17:14,870 --> 00:17:16,030
Why do you come?

146
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:19,610
White Rat, the Unsullied who...

147
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:25,010
I have heard they found his body in a brothel.

148
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:29,630
I have heard that more than one Unsullied

149
00:17:29,630 --> 00:17:32,180
has been known to visit Meereen's brothels.

150
00:17:35,150 --> 00:17:36,650
May I ask you why?

151
00:17:38,690 --> 00:17:40,860
Why would an Unsullied go to a brothel?

152
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,580
I do not know.

153
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,280
I must go.

154
00:18:07,130 --> 00:18:08,990
- Get your shield up. - It's too heavy.

155
00:18:08,990 --> 00:18:10,410
If it wasn't heavy, it wouldn't stop a sword.

156
00:18:10,410 --> 00:18:11,450
Now get it up.

157
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,690
Come. Try it again.

158
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:29,750
Drive at me. Keep your shield up.

159
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,640
Or I'll ring your head like a bell.

160
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,340
Shouldn't you be training, too?

161
00:18:35,930 --> 00:18:38,630
I'm hardly a new recruit.

162
00:18:41,230 --> 00:18:42,390
How many brothers can say

163
00:18:42,390 --> 00:18:44,410
that they've killed a white walker and a Thenn?

164
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:46,560
I might be the first in history.

165
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,210
These men need a firm hand.

166
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:50,780
Always have.

167
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:53,070
They're poachers and thieves.

168
00:18:55,490 --> 00:18:57,010
Not soldiers.

169
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:04,670
That one hates me.

170
00:19:06,870 --> 00:19:09,390
If Ser Alliser is chosen as the new Lord Commander...

171
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:11,560
He hates the wildlings.

172
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,580
All the wildlings.

173
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:16,900
- Don't let them send us away. - It's not a sure thing.

174
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:20,090
Ser Denys Mallister has commanded the Shadow Tower for 20 years

175
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,480
and people say he's a good man.

176
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,710
He's running against Ser Alliser...

177
00:19:22,710 --> 00:19:25,500
Sam, don't let them send us away.

178
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:26,630
I told you.

179
00:19:27,650 --> 00:19:30,070
Wherever you go, I go, too.

180
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:32,200
You can't leave. They'll execute you.

181
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,090
Good, good, pivot. Don't forget to pivot.

182
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:44,790
Shield up.

183
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,800
The king wants a word.

184
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:18,990
You're not cold, my lady?

185
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:20,660
Never.

186
00:20:22,190 --> 00:20:24,770
The Lord's fire lives within me, Jon Snow.

187
00:20:28,030 --> 00:20:28,710
Feel.

188
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,180
Are you a virgin?

189
00:20:42,770 --> 00:20:43,400
No.

190
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:47,020
Good.

191
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:55,710
Your Grace.

192
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,330
The bastard of Winterfell.

193
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,970
You know who rules at Winterfell now?

194
00:21:11,590 --> 00:21:12,630
Roose Bolton.

195
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:16,090
The traitor who plunged a dagger in Robb Stark's heart.

196
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:19,290
Don't you want to avenge him?

197
00:21:20,930 --> 00:21:23,140
I want a great many things, Your Grace.

198
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:26,370
But I'm a sworn brother of the Night's Watch now.

199
00:21:26,890 --> 00:21:28,860
I've been talking to your sworn brothers.

200
00:21:29,980 --> 00:21:31,720
- Many of them love you. - They're good men.

201
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,580
Many don't.

202
00:21:33,710 --> 00:21:37,360
You were seen taking the body of a wildling girl north of the Wall.

203
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:38,630
Why?

204
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:40,300
It's where she belonged.

205
00:21:40,730 --> 00:21:42,450
Some of the Night's Watch feel you have

206
00:21:42,470 --> 00:21:44,220
too much affection for the wildlings.

207
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:46,170
They were born on the wrong side of the Wall.

208
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,940
That doesn't make them monsters.

209
00:21:49,310 --> 00:21:50,050
No matter.

210
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:53,180
I shall take back the North from the thieves who stole it.

211
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:55,640
Tywin Lannister is dead. He can't protect them now.

212
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:58,950
I shall mount Roose Bolton's head on a spike.

213
00:21:59,850 --> 00:22:02,060
But if I'm to take Winterfell, I need more men.

214
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:05,030
The men of the Night's Watch are sworn to play no part--

215
00:22:05,030 --> 00:22:06,930
I'm not talking about the damn Night's Watch.

216
00:22:07,030 --> 00:22:08,470
I'm talking about the wildlings.

217
00:22:17,730 --> 00:22:20,810
Your Grace, you want the wildlings

218
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,360
to march in your army?

219
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,740
If they swear to follow me, I'll pardon them.

220
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:26,650
We'll take Winterfell. Once the North is won,

221
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:28,590
I'll declare them citizens of the realm.

222
00:22:28,700 --> 00:22:30,140
I'll give them land to live on.

223
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:33,560
It's a fair offer. More than fair.

224
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,860
I'll offer them their lives and their freedom

225
00:22:36,210 --> 00:22:39,070
if Mance kneels before me and swears his loyalty.

226
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:40,900
I don't think that's likely.

227
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:44,570
You admire him, don't you?

228
00:22:44,570 --> 00:22:46,950
- I respect him. - He likes you.

229
00:22:47,310 --> 00:22:49,170
- Convince him to bend the knee... - Your Grace.

230
00:22:49,170 --> 00:22:50,340
or he burns.

231
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:55,830
How much time do I have?

232
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:57,100
Nightfall.

233
00:22:57,650 --> 00:22:59,750
The sun drops fast this time of year.

234
00:22:59,930 --> 00:23:01,350
Hurry, Jon Snow.

235
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:05,970
Shield up.

236
00:23:07,390 --> 00:23:08,910
Attack, my lord!

237
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:10,660
Attack!

238
00:23:11,810 --> 00:23:13,380
Don't cross your feet.

239
00:23:14,550 --> 00:23:16,120
My sons had swords in their hands

240
00:23:16,130 --> 00:23:18,060
from the time they could walk. This one...

241
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:20,100
Lord Arryn will never be a great warrior.

242
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:21,350
Great warrior?

243
00:23:22,030 --> 00:23:24,690
He swings a sword like a girl with palsy.

244
00:23:24,690 --> 00:23:25,540
My lord.

245
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:29,530
Sword up, my lord!

246
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:39,100
Some boys develop more slowly.

247
00:23:40,180 --> 00:23:41,290
He's still young.

248
00:23:41,290 --> 00:23:44,290
He's 13. Boys go to war at 13.

249
00:23:44,290 --> 00:23:46,200
- He has other gifts. - Does he?

250
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,420
The gift of a great name.

251
00:23:49,230 --> 00:23:52,620
Sometimes that's all one needs.

252
00:23:57,970 --> 00:24:00,560
Good-bye, Lord Royce, and thank you for all you've done for me.

253
00:24:00,560 --> 00:24:02,970
I have done nothing more than my duty, my lady.

254
00:24:03,050 --> 00:24:04,490
I have no doubt that on my return,

255
00:24:04,490 --> 00:24:07,100
Robin's skills will have improved immeasurably.

256
00:24:07,820 --> 00:24:09,190
He'll be safe here.

257
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:11,950
As for his skills,

258
00:24:12,530 --> 00:24:14,270
I make no promises.

259
00:24:27,710 --> 00:24:29,270
Will we head north at some point?

260
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:33,540
He said Sansa had a brother at Castle Black.

261
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:36,410
We're a few days' ride from the Kingsroad.

262
00:24:36,730 --> 00:24:38,730
- But that will take us-- - Us?

263
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:43,290
The only reason you're here is because Jaime Lannister

264
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:45,440
told me you weren't safe in the capital.

265
00:24:47,440 --> 00:24:49,530
You're hundreds of miles from King's Landing.

266
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:51,930
No one knows what you look like.

267
00:24:52,290 --> 00:24:55,340
No one cares. You're safe.

268
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:57,980
- But I'm your squire. - Do you even know what a squire is?

269
00:25:00,390 --> 00:25:01,590
An attendant to a knight.

270
00:25:01,590 --> 00:25:02,700
I'm not a knight.

271
00:25:03,180 --> 00:25:04,700
That means you're not a squire.

272
00:25:05,730 --> 00:25:06,680
Well, where would I go?

273
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,800
I don't care. I'm not your mother.

274
00:25:18,220 --> 00:25:20,200
You swore to find the Stark girls.

275
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:23,040
I found Arya. She didn't want my protection.

276
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:25,260
- Sansa still might. - Will you shut your mouth?

277
00:25:26,290 --> 00:25:27,920
I didn't ask for your advice.

278
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:32,460
I don't want anyone following me.

279
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,120
I'm not a leader.

280
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:37,500
All I ever wanted was to fight for a lord I believed in.

281
00:25:38,190 --> 00:25:40,490
The good lords are dead and the rest are monsters.

282
00:25:51,380 --> 00:25:53,900
You told Lord Royce we were going to the Fingers.

283
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:54,760
I did.

284
00:25:56,320 --> 00:25:59,040
- But we're heading west. - We are.

285
00:25:59,430 --> 00:26:01,600
If he wanted to betray us, he already would have.

286
00:26:03,450 --> 00:26:06,230
Lord Royce might be as honorable as he thinks he is,

287
00:26:06,530 --> 00:26:08,200
but he's not alone in that castle.

288
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:10,930
Do you trust all those knights and ladies,

289
00:26:10,930 --> 00:26:13,060
stable boys and serving girls?

290
00:26:13,060 --> 00:26:16,400
No, do you trust the carriage driver or the knights escorting us?

291
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:17,300
No.

292
00:26:18,670 --> 00:26:19,920
But I pay them well

293
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:22,450
and they've seen what happens to men who disappoint me.

294
00:26:22,450 --> 00:26:23,960
So where are we going?

295
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,840
To a land where you trust everyone?

296
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:29,680
To a land so far from here,

297
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:32,610
even Cersei Lannister can't get her hands on you.

298
00:26:40,650 --> 00:26:44,040
It was such a deep, deep shock to us all.

299
00:26:47,660 --> 00:26:48,770
Your father was a--

300
00:26:49,550 --> 00:26:51,460
a force to be reckoned with.

301
00:26:51,850 --> 00:26:52,830
He truly was.

302
00:26:54,050 --> 00:26:57,580
I wouldn't presume to claim to have known him as such, but--

303
00:26:58,400 --> 00:27:01,240
but just being in his presence was enough to make it so clear

304
00:27:01,770 --> 00:27:04,870
just how formidable a person you were dealing with.

305
00:27:05,060 --> 00:27:08,600
What a-- what a force to be reckoned with.

306
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:12,210
Thank you so much for your kind words.

307
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:19,410
Deepest condolences, Your Grace.

308
00:27:19,410 --> 00:27:22,330
This tragedy... I never trusted Varys.

309
00:27:22,330 --> 00:27:23,590
I often warned...

310
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:29,620
Your Grace.

311
00:27:32,210 --> 00:27:34,800
Cousin Lancel. I hardly recognized you.

312
00:27:34,800 --> 00:27:36,090
My deepest sympathies.

313
00:27:37,550 --> 00:27:40,050
I apologize for my son's appearance.

314
00:27:40,260 --> 00:27:41,780
Uncle, that's quite all right.

315
00:27:44,740 --> 00:27:46,710
They call themselves sparrows.

316
00:27:47,520 --> 00:27:48,980
Bloody fanatics.

317
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:51,520
Religion has its place, of course,

318
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:52,860
but at a certain point...

319
00:27:54,270 --> 00:27:57,060
They never would have come to the capital when Tywin was alive.

320
00:27:57,060 --> 00:27:58,850
I'm sure he'll grow out of it,

321
00:27:59,050 --> 00:28:00,080
whatever it is.

322
00:28:01,260 --> 00:28:02,950
- Excuse me. - Of course.

323
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:24,440
Your wounds from the Blackwater seem to have healed.

324
00:28:25,500 --> 00:28:27,740
It wasn't my wounds that needed healing.

325
00:28:30,630 --> 00:28:31,800
What can I do for you?

326
00:28:33,910 --> 00:28:35,030
You can forgive me.

327
00:28:35,900 --> 00:28:38,730
What could you possibly have done to warrant my forgiveness?

328
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:41,190
I led you into the darkness.

329
00:28:41,300 --> 00:28:43,180
I doubt you've ever led anyone anywhere.

330
00:28:43,830 --> 00:28:45,560
I tempted you into our...

331
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:48,550
unnatural relations.

332
00:28:50,260 --> 00:28:53,430
And, of course, there was the king...

333
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:56,790
his boar hunt.

334
00:28:59,500 --> 00:29:00,340
His wine.

335
00:29:04,270 --> 00:29:05,660
I don't know what you're talking about.

336
00:29:07,320 --> 00:29:08,930
I'm a different person now.

337
00:29:10,930 --> 00:29:13,880
I've found peace in the light of the Seven.

338
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:15,190
You can, too.

339
00:29:15,270 --> 00:29:16,720
They watch over all of us,

340
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,650
ready to dole out mercy

341
00:29:20,030 --> 00:29:21,060
or justice.

342
00:29:24,760 --> 00:29:26,580
Their world is at hand.

343
00:29:29,590 --> 00:29:31,380
I will pray for your father's soul.

344
00:29:33,940 --> 00:29:37,160
The day Tywin Lannister's soul needs your help...

345
00:29:45,950 --> 00:29:48,850
- It looks like Dorne. - It doesn't.

346
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:50,550
It does.

347
00:29:51,650 --> 00:29:55,600
That's the-- that's the Sunspear bit right there.

348
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:58,700
And that's where the mountains are.

349
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:00,910
And over here is--

350
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:04,630
is Sunsnake?

351
00:30:05,090 --> 00:30:06,130
Stonespear?

352
00:30:06,140 --> 00:30:07,180
Sandstone.

353
00:30:07,990 --> 00:30:08,690
Yes.

354
00:30:09,470 --> 00:30:11,200
Yes, Sandstone.

355
00:30:13,370 --> 00:30:14,330
Just there.

356
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:15,950
Fine.

357
00:30:19,470 --> 00:30:20,340
It's Dorne.

358
00:30:22,340 --> 00:30:23,310
We should go there.

359
00:30:24,510 --> 00:30:27,350
I think we would have a lovely time,

360
00:30:27,650 --> 00:30:29,700
judging by my experience.

361
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:33,170
That would be wonderful. Dorne, Highgarden.

362
00:30:34,230 --> 00:30:35,380
Anywhere but here.

363
00:30:44,950 --> 00:30:46,730
We're late for dinner as it is.

364
00:30:47,940 --> 00:30:48,940
You're very respectful.

365
00:30:48,940 --> 00:30:50,170
I'm very hungry.

366
00:31:07,810 --> 00:31:08,890
What's your name?

367
00:31:10,380 --> 00:31:11,670
Olyvar, my lady.

368
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:17,080
I'm afraid my brother is keeping the king waiting, Olyvar.

369
00:31:26,630 --> 00:31:27,310
My lady.

370
00:31:41,570 --> 00:31:44,900
Perhaps you might consider being a bit more discreet?

371
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:46,060
Why?

372
00:31:46,990 --> 00:31:48,570
They all know about me anyway.

373
00:31:49,380 --> 00:31:51,720
Everybody knows everything about everyone.

374
00:31:52,470 --> 00:31:54,570
What's the point in trying to keep a secret in a place like this?

375
00:31:54,570 --> 00:31:58,160
In any event, you shouldn't keep your intended waiting.

376
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:01,630
My intended? Please.

377
00:32:01,630 --> 00:32:02,620
Tywin's dead.

378
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:05,110
That means no one can force Cersei to marry me.

379
00:32:05,110 --> 00:32:07,010
- Lucky you. - Unlucky you.

380
00:32:07,010 --> 00:32:09,360
You think I want that woman married to my brother?

381
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:12,620
If she doesn't marry me, she doesn't go to Highgarden.

382
00:32:13,090 --> 00:32:15,060
Which means she stays in King's Landing.

383
00:32:15,410 --> 00:32:16,690
Which means you're trapped here

384
00:32:16,690 --> 00:32:19,180
with Cersei Lannister as your mother by law.

385
00:32:19,830 --> 00:32:20,620
Perhaps.

386
00:32:22,150 --> 00:32:22,950
Perhaps?

387
00:32:24,320 --> 00:32:25,110
Perhaps.

388
00:32:39,410 --> 00:32:43,660
Eunuch, the Spider, the Master of Whisperers.

389
00:32:43,660 --> 00:32:45,470
Imp, Half-man.

390
00:32:48,390 --> 00:32:50,330
There are faster ways to kill yourself.

391
00:32:50,330 --> 00:32:51,530
Not for a coward.

392
00:32:52,260 --> 00:32:54,000
You are many things, my friend,

393
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,400
but not a coward.

394
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:01,980
You never told me why you set me free.

395
00:33:02,470 --> 00:33:03,900
Your brother asked me to.

396
00:33:05,500 --> 00:33:06,480
Could have said no.

397
00:33:07,130 --> 00:33:09,490
Refuse the Kingslayer? A dangerous proposition.

398
00:33:09,490 --> 00:33:11,520
Not as dangerous as releasing me.

399
00:33:11,970 --> 00:33:14,460
You risked your life, your position, everything.

400
00:33:14,460 --> 00:33:16,910
Why? You're not family. You owe me nothing.

401
00:33:17,450 --> 00:33:19,010
I didn't do it for you.

402
00:33:19,810 --> 00:33:21,840
I did it for the Seven Kingdoms.

403
00:33:21,890 --> 00:33:25,340
A drunken dwarf will never be the savior of the Seven Kingdoms.

404
00:33:25,340 --> 00:33:27,090
I don't believe in saviors.

405
00:33:27,320 --> 00:33:31,090
I believe men of talent have a part to play in the war to come.

406
00:33:32,350 --> 00:33:34,380
You're going to have to find another soldier.

407
00:33:35,430 --> 00:33:38,580
I'm done with Westeros and Westeros is done with me.

408
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:41,350
You have many admirable qualities,

409
00:33:41,350 --> 00:33:43,100
self-pity is not one of them.

410
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:45,240
Any fool with a bit of luck

411
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:47,980
can find himself born into power.

412
00:33:48,590 --> 00:33:52,460
But earning it for yourself, that takes work.

413
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:54,720
I'm not well-suited for work.

414
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:55,730
I think you are.

415
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:58,900
You have your father's instincts for politics.

416
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,200
And you have compassion.

417
00:34:00,200 --> 00:34:02,110
Compassion? Yes.

418
00:34:03,530 --> 00:34:06,690
I killed my lover with my bare hands.

419
00:34:06,900 --> 00:34:10,120
I shot my own father with a crossbow.

420
00:34:10,120 --> 00:34:12,020
I never said you were perfect.

421
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:15,600
What is it you want exactly?

422
00:34:16,060 --> 00:34:17,210
Peace.

423
00:34:18,210 --> 00:34:19,610
Prosperity.

424
00:34:20,060 --> 00:34:23,470
A land where the powerful do not prey on the powerless.

425
00:34:23,470 --> 00:34:25,580
Where the castles are made of gingerbread

426
00:34:25,590 --> 00:34:28,570
and the moats are filled with blackberry wine.

427
00:34:28,570 --> 00:34:30,810
The powerful have always preyed on the powerless.

428
00:34:30,810 --> 00:34:33,240
That's how they became powerful in the first place.

429
00:34:33,240 --> 00:34:34,450
Perhaps.

430
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:38,250
And perhaps we've grown so used to horror,

431
00:34:38,420 --> 00:34:40,600
we assume there's no other way.

432
00:34:41,690 --> 00:34:43,880
If you sat on the Iron Throne,

433
00:34:43,890 --> 00:34:46,240
would you spread misery throughout the land?

434
00:34:46,240 --> 00:34:48,690
I will never sit on the Iron Throne.

435
00:34:48,970 --> 00:34:50,520
No, you won't.

436
00:34:50,850 --> 00:34:53,410
But you could help another climb those steps

437
00:34:53,410 --> 00:34:55,280
and take that seat.

438
00:34:56,100 --> 00:34:59,090
The Seven Kingdoms need someone stronger than Tommen,

439
00:34:59,090 --> 00:35:01,090
but gentler than Stannis.

440
00:35:01,300 --> 00:35:02,900
A monarch who can intimidate

441
00:35:02,900 --> 00:35:05,210
the high lords and inspire the people.

442
00:35:05,210 --> 00:35:07,970
A ruler loved by millions with a powerful army

443
00:35:07,970 --> 00:35:10,150
and the right family name.

444
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:12,050
Good luck finding him.

445
00:35:13,140 --> 00:35:15,350
Who said anything about "Him"?

446
00:35:19,430 --> 00:35:21,440
You have a choice, my friend.

447
00:35:21,470 --> 00:35:23,970
You can stay here at Illyrio's palace

448
00:35:23,970 --> 00:35:25,930
and drink yourself to death,

449
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:28,470
or you can ride with me to Meereen,

450
00:35:28,470 --> 00:35:29,890
meet Daenerys Targaryen,

451
00:35:29,890 --> 00:35:32,970
and decide if the world is worth fighting for.

452
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:38,890
Can I drink myself to death on the road to Meereen?

453
00:35:49,380 --> 00:35:52,250
When did the Unsullied start patrolling the streets of Meereen?

454
00:35:52,260 --> 00:35:55,140
Looks like your friends haven't been behaving themselves.

455
00:35:58,040 --> 00:36:01,090
Our mission to Yunkai was a resounding success.

456
00:36:01,090 --> 00:36:03,490
The Wise Masters of Yunkai have agreed to cede power

457
00:36:03,490 --> 00:36:05,270
to a council of elders made up of

458
00:36:05,270 --> 00:36:07,930
both the freed men and the former slaveholders.

459
00:36:07,930 --> 00:36:11,000
All matters of consequence will be brought to you for review.

460
00:36:11,180 --> 00:36:12,310
Good.

461
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:14,960
They did ask for some concessions.

462
00:36:15,490 --> 00:36:16,890
Concessions?

463
00:36:17,020 --> 00:36:19,220
Politics is the art of compromise, Your Grace.

464
00:36:19,220 --> 00:36:20,810
I'm not a politician.

465
00:36:20,810 --> 00:36:22,070
I'm a queen.

466
00:36:22,650 --> 00:36:23,720
Forgive me.

467
00:36:23,980 --> 00:36:25,350
You're right, of course.

468
00:36:25,350 --> 00:36:29,760
Still, it's easier to rule happy subjects than angry ones.

469
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:32,000
I don't expect the Wise Masters to be happy.

470
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,690
Slavery made them rich.

471
00:36:33,860 --> 00:36:35,190
I ended slavery.

472
00:36:35,190 --> 00:36:37,680
They do not ask for the return of slavery.

473
00:36:38,120 --> 00:36:41,100
They ask for the reopening of the fighting pits.

474
00:36:42,090 --> 00:36:43,540
The fighting pits?

475
00:36:43,590 --> 00:36:46,060
Where slaves fought slaves to the death?

476
00:36:46,060 --> 00:36:48,080
In the new world that you've brought to us,

477
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:50,330
free men would fight free men.

478
00:36:51,790 --> 00:36:53,190
The pit fighters you liberated

479
00:36:53,190 --> 00:36:55,110
plead for this opportunity.

480
00:36:55,710 --> 00:36:57,660
Bring some here and ask them yourself.

481
00:36:57,660 --> 00:36:59,120
No fighting pits.

482
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:00,660
Opening them would show the people of

483
00:37:00,660 --> 00:37:03,210
Yunkai and Meereen that you respect their traditions.

484
00:37:03,210 --> 00:37:06,130
I do not respect the tradition of human cockfighting.

485
00:37:06,130 --> 00:37:07,860
- If you-- - How many times must I say no

486
00:37:07,860 --> 00:37:09,590
before you understand?

487
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:14,120
Whatever he wants from me, he's not going to get it.

488
00:37:14,430 --> 00:37:17,000
If he really believes I'm going to reopen the fighting pits...

489
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,960
You should reopen the fighting pits.

490
00:37:20,660 --> 00:37:21,740
What?

491
00:37:22,390 --> 00:37:24,920
My mother was a whore. I told you that.

492
00:37:26,950 --> 00:37:28,990
She liked to drink pear brandy.

493
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:30,650
The older she got,

494
00:37:30,930 --> 00:37:32,440
the less she made selling her body,

495
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:34,110
the more she wanted to drink.

496
00:37:35,070 --> 00:37:38,070
So one day when I was 12, she sold me to a slaver

497
00:37:38,080 --> 00:37:40,010
she fucked the night before.

498
00:37:41,410 --> 00:37:42,600
I'm sorry.

499
00:37:43,100 --> 00:37:46,160
Why? I was a bad child.

500
00:37:46,170 --> 00:37:49,570
I wasn't big, but I was quick.

501
00:37:49,630 --> 00:37:51,020
And I loved to fight.

502
00:37:51,020 --> 00:37:52,910
So they sold me to a man in Tolos

503
00:37:52,910 --> 00:37:55,010
who trained fighters for the pits.

504
00:37:55,380 --> 00:37:57,940
I had my first match when I was 16.

505
00:37:58,040 --> 00:37:59,550
You were sold into slavery,

506
00:37:59,550 --> 00:38:00,860
forced to fight to the death

507
00:38:00,860 --> 00:38:02,270
for the amusement of the masters,

508
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,200
and you're defending the fighting pits?

509
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:08,310
I'm only here because of those pits.

510
00:38:08,310 --> 00:38:10,780
I learned to fight like a Dothraki screamer,

511
00:38:10,780 --> 00:38:13,370
a Norvoshi priest, a Westerosi knight.

512
00:38:13,370 --> 00:38:14,980
Soon I was famous.

513
00:38:14,980 --> 00:38:17,230
10,000 men and women screamed my name

514
00:38:17,230 --> 00:38:18,890
when I stepped into the pit.

515
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:20,910
I made so much money for my master,

516
00:38:20,930 --> 00:38:23,180
he set me free when he died.

517
00:38:23,450 --> 00:38:25,550
I joined the Second Sons.

518
00:38:25,750 --> 00:38:27,110
And then I met you.

519
00:38:33,320 --> 00:38:34,710
You're the queen.

520
00:38:35,300 --> 00:38:37,890
Everyone's too afraid of you to speak truth.

521
00:38:38,150 --> 00:38:39,760
Everyone but me.

522
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:44,460
You've made thousands of enemies all across the world.

523
00:38:44,460 --> 00:38:47,180
As soon as they see weakness,

524
00:38:47,190 --> 00:38:48,650
they'll attack.

525
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:53,080
Show your strength here, now.

526
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:55,680
That's why I have the Unsullied patrolling the streets.

527
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:59,380
Anyone with a chest full of gold

528
00:38:59,390 --> 00:39:01,470
can buy an army of Unsullied.

529
00:39:01,470 --> 00:39:03,950
You're not the Mother of Unsullied.

530
00:39:05,020 --> 00:39:06,940
You're the Mother of Dragons.

531
00:39:13,830 --> 00:39:17,230
I don't want another child's bones dropped at my feet.

532
00:39:18,660 --> 00:39:20,780
No one's seen Drogon in weeks.

533
00:39:21,390 --> 00:39:24,010
For all I know, he's flown halfway across the world.

534
00:39:28,930 --> 00:39:30,590
I can't control them anymore.

535
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:34,960
A dragon queen with no dragons

536
00:39:36,270 --> 00:39:37,530
is not a queen.

537
00:40:43,860 --> 00:40:45,110
Viserion?

538
00:40:48,050 --> 00:40:49,240
Rhaegal?

539
00:41:01,710 --> 00:41:03,580
Easy. Easy.

540
00:41:03,590 --> 00:41:04,660
Easy.

541
00:41:45,060 --> 00:41:46,430
So here we are.

542
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:48,280
Here we are.

543
00:41:51,380 --> 00:41:53,890
When we first met, you were my prisoner.

544
00:41:54,900 --> 00:41:57,750
And now, for our last meeting...

545
00:42:00,250 --> 00:42:02,600
This doesn't have to be our last meeting.

546
00:42:02,600 --> 00:42:05,230
No, but it will be.

547
00:42:07,540 --> 00:42:09,240
You know what Stannis wants?

548
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:11,880
He wants me to bend the knee.

549
00:42:12,620 --> 00:42:14,980
And he wants the free folk to fight for him.

550
00:42:16,060 --> 00:42:17,790
I'll give him this much,

551
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,130
he's bold.

552
00:42:19,320 --> 00:42:21,120
Shouldn't a king be bold?

553
00:42:21,240 --> 00:42:22,500
Oh, aye.

554
00:42:23,450 --> 00:42:25,020
I respect him.

555
00:42:26,170 --> 00:42:27,660
If he gets what he wants,

556
00:42:27,660 --> 00:42:29,350
I expect he'll be a better ruler than

557
00:42:29,350 --> 00:42:32,790
the fools sitting on the Iron Throne the last hundred years.

558
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:35,270
But I'll never serve him.

559
00:42:37,270 --> 00:42:38,770
You told me you weren't here to conquer.

560
00:42:38,770 --> 00:42:40,100
You told me your people have bled enough.

561
00:42:40,100 --> 00:42:41,130
That's right.

562
00:42:42,280 --> 00:42:44,860
I don't want them bleeding for Stannis Baratheon either.

563
00:42:44,860 --> 00:42:48,200
You spent your life convincing 90 clans to come together

564
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:50,190
for the first time in history.

565
00:42:50,610 --> 00:42:52,450
Thenns and Hornfoots,

566
00:42:52,720 --> 00:42:55,260
the ice-river clans, even the giants.

567
00:42:55,880 --> 00:42:57,780
A life's work uniting them.

568
00:42:57,780 --> 00:42:59,320
You didn't do it for power.

569
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:01,420
You didn't do it for glory.

570
00:43:02,350 --> 00:43:04,360
You brought them together to save them

571
00:43:04,370 --> 00:43:06,080
because none of them will survive the winter,

572
00:43:06,080 --> 00:43:07,680
not if they're north of the Wall.

573
00:43:07,680 --> 00:43:10,330
Isn't their survival more important than your pride?

574
00:43:10,330 --> 00:43:11,510
Pride?

575
00:43:14,090 --> 00:43:16,020
Fuck my pride.

576
00:43:18,490 --> 00:43:20,240
This isn't about that.

577
00:43:22,340 --> 00:43:26,180
Then bend the knee and save your people.

578
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:31,180
They followed me because they respected me.

579
00:43:31,230 --> 00:43:32,970
Because they believed in me.

580
00:43:32,970 --> 00:43:35,340
The moment I kneel for a southern king, that's all gone.

581
00:43:35,340 --> 00:43:38,290
And how many tens of thousands are out there right now?

582
00:43:38,690 --> 00:43:41,540
How many women? How many children?

583
00:43:41,870 --> 00:43:44,490
And you won't go out and rescue them because why?

584
00:43:45,340 --> 00:43:47,560
You're afraid of looking afraid.

585
00:43:47,570 --> 00:43:50,500
Oh, I am afraid.

586
00:43:51,620 --> 00:43:53,350
No shame in that.

587
00:44:02,610 --> 00:44:03,900
How will they do it?

588
00:44:04,310 --> 00:44:05,450
Beheading?

589
00:44:06,580 --> 00:44:07,670
Hanging?

590
00:44:11,870 --> 00:44:13,490
They'll burn you alive.

591
00:44:18,310 --> 00:44:19,680
Bad way to go.

592
00:44:23,970 --> 00:44:25,410
I'll be honest with you.

593
00:44:25,770 --> 00:44:27,570
I don't want to die.

594
00:44:28,080 --> 00:44:29,470
And burnt to death,

595
00:44:29,580 --> 00:44:31,950
I don't want people to remember me like that,

596
00:44:31,950 --> 00:44:34,130
scorched and screaming.

597
00:44:34,920 --> 00:44:38,240
But it's better than betraying everything I believe.

598
00:44:38,890 --> 00:44:40,750
And what happens to your people?

599
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:44,110
You preserve your dignity and die standing

600
00:44:44,590 --> 00:44:46,540
and they'll sing songs about you.

601
00:44:47,150 --> 00:44:49,220
You'd rather burn than kneel.

602
00:44:49,380 --> 00:44:50,830
The great hero.

603
00:44:52,360 --> 00:44:53,750
Until winter comes

604
00:44:54,090 --> 00:44:55,760
and the white walkers come for us all

605
00:44:55,770 --> 00:44:57,860
and there's no one left to sing.

606
00:45:01,200 --> 00:45:02,840
You're a good lad.

607
00:45:03,400 --> 00:45:05,430
Truly you are.

608
00:45:06,380 --> 00:45:08,180
But if you can't understand

609
00:45:08,180 --> 00:45:10,590
why I won't enlist my people

610
00:45:10,600 --> 00:45:12,300
in a foreigner's war,

611
00:45:13,430 --> 00:45:15,380
there's no point explaining.

612
00:45:31,880 --> 00:45:34,360
I think you're making a terrible mistake.

613
00:45:35,640 --> 00:45:38,170
The freedom to make my own mistakes

614
00:45:38,170 --> 00:45:39,970
was all I ever wanted.

615
00:46:49,790 --> 00:46:53,140
Mance Rayder, you've been called the King-beyond-the-Wall.

616
00:46:53,140 --> 00:46:55,200
Westeros only has one king.

617
00:46:56,350 --> 00:46:58,480
Bend the knee, I promise you mercy.

618
00:47:12,170 --> 00:47:13,540
Kneel and live.

619
00:47:21,700 --> 00:47:25,110
This was my home for many years.

620
00:47:27,250 --> 00:47:29,360
I wish you good fortune

621
00:47:29,540 --> 00:47:31,170
in the wars to come.

622
00:48:13,640 --> 00:48:15,430
We all must choose.

623
00:48:16,660 --> 00:48:18,070
Man or woman,

624
00:48:18,340 --> 00:48:20,020
young or old,

625
00:48:20,120 --> 00:48:21,410
lord or peasant,

626
00:48:21,410 --> 00:48:23,330
our choices are the same.

627
00:48:23,500 --> 00:48:26,910
We choose light or we choose darkness.

628
00:48:27,290 --> 00:48:30,290
We choose good or we choose evil.

629
00:48:30,540 --> 00:48:35,100
We choose the true god or the false.

630
00:48:46,020 --> 00:48:47,360
Free folk,

631
00:48:48,270 --> 00:48:50,540
there is only one true king

632
00:48:50,650 --> 00:48:53,210
and his name is Stannis.

633
00:48:53,220 --> 00:48:55,610
Here stands your king of lies.

634
00:48:55,610 --> 00:48:58,940
Behold the fate of those who choose the darkness.

